{
  "_comment": [
    "Multi-turn conversations over the indexed Grade 6 science textbook.",
    "Single-turn evals cannot see the failure these exist to measure: a turn",
    "is only wrong relative to the turns before it.",
    "",
    "expect: answers  -> grounded, cites the syllabus, and stays on `about`",
    "        refuses  -> no citations; the syllabus does not cover it",
    "        chats    -> answered without searching at all",
    "        any      -> any non-empty reply; only its language is checked",
    "about:  a word the answer must contain, which is how continuity is checked",
    "        without asking a model whether two answers are about the same thing",
    "language: the language the reply must be in; a subject is taught in its own",
    "        language unless the student asks for another"
  ],
  "subject_id": "b9ec8535-7c88-40a2-a1a3-251a2b7cdb45",
  "lecture_id": "aaaaaaaa-0000-4000-8000-00000000f001",
  "conversations": [
    {
      "name": "a student who does not understand",
      "turns": [
        {
          "say": "Can you explain to me evaporation, please?",
          "expect": "answers",
          "about": "evaporat",
          "language": "en"
        },
        {
          "say": "Can you explain more?",
          "expect": "answers",
          "about": "evaporat",
          "language": "en"
        },
        {
          "say": "Give me an example.",
          "expect": "answers",
          "about": "evaporat",
          "language": "en"
        },
        {
          "say": "I feel that I still don't understand. Would you explain to me in layman's language, in a simpler way, maybe using bullets or making it easier for me to understand?",
          "expect": "answers",
          "about": "evaporat",
          "language": "en"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "short follow-ups",
      "turns": [
